    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "HAG",
      "chapter": 2,
      "chapter_usfm": "HAG.2",
      "version_id": 1713,
      "version_abbr": "CSB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.1",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "On the twenty-first day of the seventh month, the word of the Lord came through the prophet Haggai:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.2",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "“Speak to Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, to the high priest Joshua son of Jehozadak, and to the remnant of the people:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.3",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "‘Who is left among you who saw this house in its former glory? How does it look to you now? Doesn’t it seem to you like nothing by comparison?"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.4",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "Even so, be strong, Zerubbabel — this is the Lord’s declaration. Be strong, Joshua son of Jehozadak, high priest. Be strong, all you people of the land — this is the Lord’s declaration. Work! For I am with you — the declaration of the Lord of Armies."
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.5",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "This is the promise I made to you when you came out of Egypt, and my Spirit is present among you; don’t be afraid.’ ”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.6",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "For the Lord of Armies says this: “Once more, in a little while, I am going to shake the heavens and the earth, the sea and the dry land."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.7",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I will shake all the nations so that the treasures of all the nations will come, and I will fill this house with glory,” says the Lord of Armies."
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.8",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“The silver and gold belong to me” — this is the declaration of the Lord of Armies."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.9",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“The final glory of this house will be greater than the first,” says the Lord of Armies. “I will provide peace in this place” — this is the declaration of the Lord of Armies."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.10",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "On the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, in the second year of Darius, the word of the Lord came to the prophet Haggai:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.11",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "“This is what the Lord of Armies says: Ask the priests for a ruling."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.12",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "If a man is carrying consecrated meat in the fold of his garment, and it touches bread, stew, wine, oil, or any other food, does it become holy? ” The priests answered, “No.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.13",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Then Haggai asked, “If someone defiled by contact with a corpse touches any of these, does it become defiled? ” The priests answered, “It becomes defiled.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.14",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Then Haggai replied, “So is this people, and so is this nation before me — this is the Lord’s declaration. And so is every work of their hands; even what they offer there is defiled."
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.15",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "“Now from this day on, think carefully: Before one stone was placed on another in the Lord’s temple,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.16",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "what state were you in? When someone came to a grain heap of twenty measures, it only amounted to ten; when one came to the winepress to dip fifty measures from the vat, it only amounted to twenty."
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.17",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "I struck you — all the work of your hands — with blight, mildew, and hail, but you didn’t turn to me — this is the Lord’s declaration."
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.18",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "From this day on, think carefully; from the twenty-fourth day of the ninth month, from the day the foundation of the Lord’s temple was laid; think carefully."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.19",
          "line_type": "p",
          "text": "Is there still seed left in the granary? The vine, the fig, the pomegranate, and the olive tree have not yet produced. But from this day on I will bless you.”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 20,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.20",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "The word of the Lord came to Haggai a second time on the twenty-fourth day of the month:"
        },
        {
          "verse": 21,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.21",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "“Speak to Zerubbabel, governor of Judah: I am going to shake the heavens and the earth."
        },
        {
          "verse": 22,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.22",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "I will overturn royal thrones and destroy the power of the Gentile kingdoms. I will overturn chariots and their riders. Horses and their riders will fall, each by his brother’s sword."
        },
        {
          "verse": 23,
          "usfm": "HAG.2.23",
          "line_type": "m",
          "text": "On that day” — this is the declaration of the Lord of Armies — “I will take you, Zerubbabel son of Shealtiel, my servant” — this is the Lord’s declaration — “and make you like my signet ring, for I have chosen you.” This is the declaration of the Lord of Armies."
        }
      ],
